# Keeps code flat: early returns instead of else branches, and at most three
# indentation levels counted from the left margin (namespaces and extern blocks
# do not indent, see .clang-format).
#
# NestingThreshold counts from the function body, which is level 1, and does
# not see an enclosing class. 3 matches the rule for free functions and member
# functions defined outside their class; a member function defined inside its
# class gets one level more than the rule allows, so review catches that case.
#
# Run with scripts/lint.sh.
---
Checks: >
  -*,
  readability-else-after-return,
  readability-function-size
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '/modules/'
CheckOptions:
  readability-function-size.NestingThreshold: 3
